From: PW3 Android port
Subject: [PW3] SystemUI recents: icon cards, six to a screen, outlined

The user found recents hard to use (Test V39): 8.1's low ram layout makes each
card a square as wide as the screen, one per screen, and with task previews
disabled (0004) the cards are blank. On the white ground the cards had no
visible edge: SystemUI is drawn in software (0003, 0006), where the shadow
that should mark them is not drawn.

With RecentsConfiguration.iconCards (low ram and ro.pw3.disable_task_previews):

  * the low ram layout puts the newest six tasks in two columns and three rows,
    newest at the top left, between the status bar and the clear-all button;
    nothing scrolls, so the e-paper panel is drawn once (older tasks are not
    shown; clear all still removes them);
  * a card's body is white with the app's icon in the middle of it (the icon
    the header already loads; still no previews); its header is the app's name
    in black on white and the dismiss button (no small icon, and not the app's
    colour, an arbitrary grey on e-paper);
  * every card has the e-paper outline and corner radius (docs/design/eink-ui.md;
    SystemUI's copy of the values in res/values/pw3_eink.xml), drawn in whole
    pixels, as does the clear-all button, now black on white.

